    <summary>Offline voice dictation — hold a key, speak, release. No cloud, no API key, no subscription.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
YazSes is a free, open-source voice dictation and speech-to-text tool that runs
entirely on your own machine. Hold a key, speak, release, and the text is typed
into whatever window has focus.

Everything runs on your CPU with faster-whisper. There is no cloud service, no
API key, no account, no subscription, and no telemetry. After the speech model is
downloaded once (~141 MB), it needs no network at all — which is the point for
confidential work and air-gapped machines.

It also transcribes recordings (optionally tagging who said what) and can capture
a whole meeting into a speaker-labelled transcript with locally generated minutes.

### Notes

* The Windows build is **not code-signed yet**, so SmartScreen may warn on first launch.
* Installs per-user (no administrator rights required).
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/MSKazemi/yazses/releases/tag/v2.29.0</releaseNotes>
